At Mon, 14 Nov 2005 09:08:44 +0100,
Vincent L=F6nngren wrote:
>=20
> Sorry to bother you again. I just realised something. The only
> method I've used to determine if the MPU is there is "pmidi -l". Could
> it be that the error is with pmidi? Is there any other way to find
> out?=20

It's easier to see whether you have /proc/asound/devices and check
"raw midi".  pmidi shows the sequencer entries, which is initialized
after sequencer module is loaded.  It might be the case that snd-seq
and drivers are not loaded automatically on your system.


